The daemon architecture (job pipeline with per-job timeouts, SQLite job
history, control socket, CUPS submission via `lp`, Pusher-protocol
websocket transport with a polling fallback) is carried over from
SyncroPrint for Linux (https://github.com/ken515151/syncroprint), MIT
licensed, by the same author. The wire protocol is TechBenchHub's own
(docs/PROTOCOL.md) and shares nothing with the AutoPrintr protocol
SyncroPrint speaks.

